---
source: crates/mcp/tests/server/startup.rs
expression: instructions
---
gsttt answers what a change affects, from an index of imports and contracts (HTTP routes, GraphQL operations, gRPC methods, tables, queues, env variables) across the repository. Call impact before you edit a file that other files import or call, with the file in paths, and again with changed=true before you finish a change: it lists the files your edits reach and the tests to run, and walks only from the declarations a patch changes where the language records them. A question about one function, class, method or variable goes to impact with its name in names, beside the file in paths: the answer lists its direct callers, and asking again about a caller goes further. dependents before renaming or deleting a file; path to learn how two files are connected; contract to find who serves and who calls an endpoint. If your client lists the tools by name only, load the schema of impact before the first call. Every answer ends with what it covered and how fresh it is; when coverage names a gap, say so instead of assuming nothing is affected.
